    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00065:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "Two structures of 2-ethylpent-1-ene highlighted differently to justify that the molecule is named as a pentene, not a hexane, since the double bond is not contained in the six-carbon chain."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_07_03_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00065:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00065:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "The first structure has a 6-carbon chain with a double bond between C2-C3. The second compound has a 6-carbon chain with methyl group at C2 and double bond between C3-C4."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_07_03_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00004",
      "segmentId": "m00065:para:para-00004"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00065:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "The structures of 2-hexene, 2-methyl-3-hexene, 2-ethyl-1-pentene, and 2-methyl-1 3-butadiene. The carbon atoms are numbered in all structures."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_07_03_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00005",
      "segmentId": "m00065:para:para-00005"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00004",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00065:alt:fig-00004-alt",
          "text": "The condensed structures of two compounds. First compound: Newer naming system: 2,5-dimethylhept-3-ene and older naming system: 2,5-dimethyl-3-heptene. Second compound: Newer naming system: 3-propylhexa-1,4-diene and older naming system: 3 propyl-1,4-hexadiene."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_07_03_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
